  "rationale": "The accepted BN-fold bundle (trial-d2a4cb48d3, objective 4.181 ms vs parent 4.227 ms, quality pass) made the measured single batch=32 FP32 forward GPU-bound: in the current-revision execution_timeline capture the kernel active union is 3989.5 us inside a 4071.0 us span with only 81.5 us of launch gaps, and python_runtime shows host self-time ~0 with the wall dominated by cuda_synchronize, so only kernel-time reduction can move latency_ms. The fold also left a measurable pointwise-epilogue tax around the convolutions themselves (call-resources.json, revision 353b783e): every one of the 20 folded conv sites (17 ResNetConvLayer + 3 ResNetShortCut calls) emits an extra non-vectorized broadcast bias-add kernel because the eager cudnn path applies conv bias as a separate elementwise pass (20 kernels, 355.9 us total; the stem site fad32b28bd6e0def6ce7593e alone pays 206.6 us after its 262.4 us conv), plus 17 separate aten::relu kernels (350.9 us) and 8 residual aten::add_ kernels (77.3 us). That is ~784 us of epilogue traffic against 2974 us of actual conv kernels (scudnn/winograd/implicit_sgemm). These kernels live entirely inside the 17 ResNetConvLayer, 3 ResNetShortCut and 8 ResNetBasicLayer module boundaries (modeling_resnet.py:113-136: layer[0] conv+ReLU, layer[1] conv with activation=None, then hidden += residual, final ReLU), which is the coherent editable boundary for fusing bias and ReLU into the conv/residual epilogues. The 8 previously selected conv/shortcut groups are re-selected so the new joint bundle explicitly supersedes the whole inherited fold bundle at every site it declared, transferring its required-call coverage to the new replacements instead of composing under them.",
  "hypothesis": "Re-executing the same FP32 math with fused epilogues removes most of the 707 us of bias-add plus ReLU kernel time: (a) at the 9 ReLU-terminated conv sites, run conv+bias+ReLU as one fused execution (aten::cudnn_convolution_relu / cudnn fused bias-activation path; verified to exist in the worker torch 2.13.0+cu129 op registry) eliminating the broadcast bias-add and the separate ReLU; (b) at the 8 activation=None second convs and 3 shortcuts, emit conv without bias and carry the folded bias into a single fused residual epilogue at the owning ResNetBasicLayer boundary that computes ReLU(hidden + residual + b_conv2 + b_shortcut) in one vectorized kernel, replacing conv2's bias-add, the shortcut's bias-add, the add_ and the post-add ReLU. Expected ceiling ~0.6-0.7 ms of the 4.06 ms GPU time (up to ~16%), i.e. clean latency_ms from ~4.18 toward ~3.5-3.6; a partial outcome (only per-site fused bias+ReLU pointwise) still yields ~0.15-0.35 ms. Numerics are unchanged in exact arithmetic (same FP32 adds/ReLU, TF32 off, cudnn.benchmark off, no AMP/quantization), so assert_close at 1e-4 and exact top-1 against the reference should hold; if the fused cudnn path is unavailable or slower on any shape, the replacement falls back to the parent callable and keeps the accepted behavior. This is a hypothesis to be tested by the framework's A/B measurement, not a predicted acceptance.",
